+// TMPSP: shadow-pass probe (launcher/dev/shadow-probe.sdk.patch). tmp_sp_mode perturbs the depth-only
+// draws of the four sun-shadow cascades (render phases 0x20..0x100, a 4x MSAA D24S8 depth target, no
+// colour written) to find what their GPU time is bound by. The picture is wrong while it is on: only the
+// GPU timestamps are read. A bit mask:
+//    1  no rasterization (an empty scissor: the vertex work and the primitive setup remain)
+//    2  the viewport 16 times smaller in each direction (the pixel work almost gone, the geometry kept)
+//    4  one triangle per draw (what a draw costs by itself: state, bindings, uploads)
+//    8  no depth and no stencil writes
+//   16  half of the triangles of each draw
+//   32  no stencil test or write (the depth write stays)
+//   64  only every tmp_sp_decimate-th draw is issued (the others are left out)
+REXCVAR_DEFINE_INT32(tmp_sp_mode, 0, "GPU",
+                     "TMPSP: perturbs the sun-shadow cascade draws (bit mask, command_processor.cpp)")
+    .lifecycle(rex::cvar::Lifecycle::kHotReload);
